The following tables, consolidated from the gems spoiler, show the
base price or surcharged sale price for gems, before charisma and
Tourist modifiers.  In many cases it is possible to identify a soft
gem as valuable or as glass based on its unique price.  For instance,
a green gem costing 533 must be fluorite, after which you know that a
violet gem costing 400 must be glass.

Unless you want to exploit a bug/feature, gems can only be price-ID'd
by getting quotes to purchase a gem owned by a shopkeeper.  You can
get such quotes from shops that don't normally sell gems by throwing
the gem into the shop from the entry square.

